              "text": "**Evaluating file methods**\n\nI’m looking at the Node documentation for \"openAsBlob,\" which is stable in Node v24 and v22.17 — that seems good. It’s somewhat comparable to \"Bun.file,\" which returns a \"Blob-like\" object. Bun.file has methods like text(), json(), stream, and exists. I wonder if \"exists()\" is part of FSFile. I think I’ll propose using \"fs.promises.stat\" or \"access\" to check for existence instead."
